STEP 1 — UNDERSTAND THE TEMPLATE STRUCTURE:

Read the [STRUCTURAL HINTS FROM DOCX ANALYSIS] block embedded above.
It contains:
- Layout Style: table_based | freeflow | mixed
- Table Loops Detected: mail-merge loops with loop_variable and item_fields
- Paste Zone Headings: headings indicating large CV paste areas
- Instruction Block Paragraphs: red/italic text to be cleared, NOT data fields
- The [STRUCTURED TABLE LABEL→VALUE PAIRS] section maps each table label to its adjacent marker or blank

Use these structural hints as the PRIMARY source of truth for field classification.

---
STEP 2 — FIELD TYPE + SOURCE KIND RULES:

Every manifest entry MUST have field_type AND source_kind.

field_type options: scalar | rich_text | array_simple | array_complex | table_loop | paste_zone | instruction_block
source_kind options: merge_marker | visual_blank_slot | bullet_slots | table_loop | paste_zone | section_body | instruction_block

Rules by source_kind:

merge_marker
  → marker_text = exact string from DETECTED MARKERS (guillemet «...» or bracket [...])
  → render_locator.strategy = replace_marker

visual_blank_slot
  → table row: bold label cell, value cell is blank or says "Type text" — NO guillemet marker
  → marker_text = ""  (DO NOT invent one)
  → render_locator.strategy = fill_blank_cell_after_label
  → render_locator.label = EXACT bold label text

bullet_slots
  → repeated generic placeholder (e.g. [Type text]) under a section heading
  → field_type = array_simple
  → render_locator.strategy = replace_bullets_under_heading
  → render_locator.heading = exact section heading text

table_loop
  → «TableStart:NAME» / «TableEnd:NAME» pair detected
  → loop_variable = NAME, loop_item_fields = fields between start and end
  → render_locator.strategy = replace_marker

paste_zone
  → large section for pasting the candidate's full CV
  → marker_text = "" (unless a marker was found in that area)
  → render_locator.strategy = replace_section_body
  → render_locator.heading = heading text

instruction_block
  → human instruction text (red, italic, or quoted) — must be CLEARED, never output
  → fieldname MUST start with _instruction_
  → marker_text = verbatim instruction text
  → render_locator.strategy = clear_instruction_block

section_body
  → free-form text area (e.g. expert opinion) under a heading
  → render_locator.strategy = replace_section_body
  → render_locator.heading = section heading

---
STEP 3 — ANTI-HALLUCINATION RULES (MANDATORY):

1. marker_text MUST exactly equal one string from DETECTED MARKERS — or be EMPTY.
   NEVER invent a marker. NEVER use bold label text as marker_text.

2. [STRUCTURED TABLE LABEL→VALUE PAIRS] is your primary mapping source:
   - If VALUE/MARKER column = a guillemet «...» → use as marker_text, source_kind=merge_marker
   - If VALUE/MARKER column = [blank] or [Type text] → marker_text="", source_kind=visual_blank_slot

3. COMPLETE COVERAGE: Every item in DETECTED MARKERS must appear in exactly one entry.

4. confidence: 1.0 for exact marker match, 0.7 for visual_blank_slot with confirmed label, 0.5 for inferred.

